  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "ATAN uses x87 FPATAN directly for |x| <= 1 and FLDPI/2 - FPATAN(1, |x|) for |x| > 1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, ATAN(x) evaluates x87 FPATAN(x, 1) directly for |x| <= 1, and for |x| > 1 computes RN53(FLDPI / 2 - FPATAN(1, |x|)) in 64-bit x87 extended precision with the sign of x restored. All 181,413 full-bank ATAN rows match.",
  "status": "inferred",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence runs/w111-atan-heldout-20260929/answers.json.gz and runs/w111-asin-intermediate-20260929/answers-atan.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430), and matched on 181,413/181,413 full-bank ATAN rows.",
  "inferred": "That Excel's x87 instruction sequence is literally FPATAN(1, |x|) subtracted from FLDPI/2 across every |x| > 1 beyond the 181,413 bank rows is inferred.",
